#====================================================================
# DRAFT - doctest/Catch2 binary built from a subset of the upstream test
# target exits green with zero cases; feature-gated cases also make the
# runtime summary lower than the source scan
# contributor: W082 (wanderlust_0823)
#====================================================================

# ═══ Layer 0: 错误面 (Error Surface) ═══
id:                     DRAFT-doctest-partial-target-zero-case-false-green
trigger_tool:           test|conan|clang
phase:                  testing
error_signature:        \[doctest\] test cases: 0 \| 0 passed \| 0 failed \| 0 skipped|\[doctest\] Status: SUCCESS!|\[doctest\] assertions: 0 \| 0 passed|\[==========\] 0 tests from 0 test suites ran|\[  PASSED  \] 0 tests

# ═══ Layer 1: 识别层 (Recognition) ═══
severity:               3
category:               testing, conan-test-execution, coverage, diagnostics, detection
match_keywords:         doctest, TEST_CASE, DOCTEST_CONFIG_IMPLEMENT_WITH_MAIN, test target SOURCES, upstream test suite, zero cases, false green, feature-gated cases, list-test-cases
title:                  A test binary compiled from part of the upstream test target can exit 0 with zero cases executed

# ═══ Layer 2: 诊断层 (Diagnosis) ═══
root_cause:             In doctest and Catch2 the file that defines the framework main (DOCTEST_CONFIG_IMPLEMENT_WITH_MAIN) compiles and links on its own, and the framework registers only the translation units actually present in the binary. Running that binary reports an empty summary and exit code 0, which every build-system-level success check reads as a pass. Separately, TEST_CASEs wrapped in feature-test-macro guards (#if SEMVER_HAS_CONSTEXPR, __cpp_lib_format, __cpp_impl_three_way_comparison and similar) are preprocessed out of the registration list, so even a complete build reports a lower number than a source scan of the same tree.
affected_scope:         Any Conan recipe that runs an upstream doctest/Catch2/GoogleTest suite by compiling a hand-written file list instead of consuming the upstream test target's SOURCES, and any claim that compares a declared case count with a runtime summary line.
verification_cmd:       <test-binary> | tail -3; <test-binary> --list-test-cases | grep -cE '^[^=[:space:]]'; grep -cE '^[[:space:]]*TEST_CASE\(' <upstream-test-dir>/*.cpp

# ═══ Layer 3: 方案层 (Solution Space) ═══
rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           build-the-declared-upstream-target-and-assert-nonzero-case-count
rec_description:        Derive the compiled file list from the upstream test target itself (the SOURCES of the add_executable in test/CMakeLists.txt, minus targets that need their own configuration such as a generated-header or MSVC-only TU, and state that exclusion explicitly), never from a guessed single file. After the run, assert on the summary line rather than on the exit code: fail the build when the parsed case count is zero or when the binary registers fewer cases than the upstream target it claims to reproduce.
rec_command:            awk '/add_executable\(/{f=1} f&&/\.cpp/{print} /\)/{f=0}' <source>/test/CMakeLists.txt; <test-binary> | tee /dev/stderr | grep -qE 'test cases: [1-9][0-9]* \|'
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               conan-recipe

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      report-static-scan-count-and-explain-the-gap
fallback_description:   When a review process requires a declared case count, declare the source-scan count (^[[:space:]]*TEST_CASE\( ) and publish the measured runtime count separately, naming the guarded blocks responsible for the difference. Do not raise the language standard until the gap is re-measured: on semver 1.0.1 moving from -std=c++17 to -std=c++20 recovered exactly one of eight remaining gated cases.
fallback_command:       grep -cE '^[[:space:]]*TEST_CASE\(' <source>/test/*.cpp; <test-binary> --list-test-cases | grep -cE '^[^=[:space:]]'; grep -nE '^[[:space:]]*#if' <source>/test/*.cpp
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:          manual

forbid_1_pattern:       \{test_cpp\}|-I"[^"]*" "\$\{?src\}?/test\.cpp" -o
forbid_1_reason:        Compiling only the framework-main translation unit produces a binary that structurally cannot register cases; it is a no-op that looks like a pass.
forbid_1_consequence:   The recipe, W3 log and CI all report success for a run that executed zero upstream assertions.
forbid_2_pattern:       test cases: 0 \| 0 passed.*SUCCESS|assertions: 0 \| 0 passed.*SUCCESS
forbid_2_reason:        Accepting an empty summary as evidence turns the exit code into a coverage claim the binary never made.
forbid_2_consequence:   A false upstream-test count gets recorded in the archive and repeated by every later consumer of the recipe.
forbid_3_pattern:       declared.*=.*grep -c|少报|report.*runtime.*summary.*as.*total
forbid_3_reason:        The runtime summary is not an upper bound on the source's case count, because feature-gated TEST_CASEs are preprocessed out; using it as the declared total under-reports real coverage.
forbid_3_consequence:   Review verdicts flip on compiler version and standard level rather than on the code under test.

# ═══ Layer 4: 原则引用 ═══
principles:             []

